from mk import mk
mk("_6mEzWHoxKo","DevOcean Modular - Create A Wind Noodle Patch From Scratch #modularsynth  #sounddesign  #synthesiser",
 "generative-wind-noise-three-filters-slow-lfos-lfo-modulated-vca-mix",
 "Generative 'noodle' wind with no MIDI: one noise source into three parallel filters (slow-swept LP, high resonant BP whistle, mid SVF BP), slightly different free-running sine LFOs with light LFO cross-mod, and an LFO-modulated three-VCA mixer",
 "Patch a self-running wind ambience bed that moves without MIDI. Split one white-noise source into three filters: a low-pass swept by a very slow sine LFO (dark rumble that brightens and darkens); a band-pass set very high with resonance pulled well up but short of self-oscillation (resonant whistle); and a mellower state-variable band-pass in the middle. Give each filter its own very slow free-running sine LFO at slightly different rates, and let one LFO lightly modulate another. Mix through a three-channel mixer whose per-channel VCA inputs are driven by three more slow sine LFOs, centred so the layers drift in and out without ever disappearing. Finish with a bracket EQ to tame and a big wash reverb. For a generative noise layer under cinematic pads, this differs from our triple-bandpass pad, which filters a played saw, and from the recorded-whoosh skill.",
 ["Noise generator, three filters (LP, resonant BP, SVF BP), six free-running LFOs, a mixer with per-channel modulation/VCA inputs (Web Audio: AudioBufferSource noise → 3 BiquadFilterNodes → GainNodes driven by OscillatorNode LFOs, implementation note)","EQ and a long reverb"],
 [("noise","audio","White noise (static on its own)",True),("lfo_rates","number[]","Very slow, deliberately unequal rates",False)],
 [("wind_bed","audio","Continuously moving wind texture that needs no notes")],
 ["Rates, cutoffs and resonance are set by ear; the transcript names no numbers. Keep all LFOs very slow and slightly different.","Keep BP resonance high but not at self-oscillation: you want a whistle, not a tone.","Mixer modulation should be centred so layers move in and out but never go fully silent.","Sine, triangle and smooth-random LFOs give flowing wind; saws and squares make it rhythmic."],
 [("Start a patch with output, a gain mixer and an EQ (disconnected). Add a white-noise oscillator at low volume, with a little extra gain on the noise module.","source","Static white noise"),
  ("Channel 1: noise → low-pass, fairly closed. Add a very slow free-running sine LFO (no MIDI, no retrigger) to its cutoff, slowed further if needed.","ch1 LP","Dark rippling wind that slowly brightens and darkens"),
  ("Channel 2: same noise → band-pass (RBJ-type) set very high, resonance pulled way up but not to a tone, to make a resonating whistle. Add its own slow LFO.","ch2 BP","High whistling layer that drifts"),
  ("Channel 3: same noise → state-variable band-pass in the middle range, a mellower flavour, with its own slow LFO.","ch3 SVF","Mid-band airy layer"),
  ("Make all three LFO rates slightly different, still very slow, and let one LFO modulate another 'just a touch'.","lfo offsets","Filters never move in sync"),
  ("Mix the three channels in a 3-input mixer with per-channel modulation inputs (each channel = a VCA), in attenuation mode, bipolar depth set in the correct direction. Drive each modulation input with its own slow sine LFO at a different speed, positioned in the middle so channels go in and out but don't disappear.","vca mix","Layers swell and recede independently"),
  ("Add a bracket (low/high-cut) EQ to tame the bed, then a big wash reverb. Save it as a patch, then explore by changing LFO rates and shapes on both filters and mixers.","fx","Immersive, self-moving wind ambience")],
 ["Patch evolves for minutes with no MIDI input.","Soloing each channel reveals a distinct band (low rumble, high whistle, mid air).","No two filter sweeps peak at the same time over a long listen.","No channel ever drops to full silence in the mix."],
 ["noise","wind","generative","ambience","bandpass","lfo","vca","modular","web-audio"],
 note="Modular app walkthrough; route.py said COVERED but hand-check found no generative noise/wind bed skill. Factory patch names omitted.")

mk("LeChNmmtNsM","Airglow Walkthrough: A High-End Atmosphere Instrument for Ambient Music",
 "scale-locked-high-end-sparkle-layer-random-notes-air-dust-noise",
 "Scale-locked high-end atmosphere layer: sporadic random note 'sprays' (sine-like and brighter 'glass' voices) above ~3 kHz with a gravity/rate control, plus pitch-locked air and dust noise layers on random-drift LFO levels and a long reverb",
 "Fill the empty 3 kHz–20 kHz zone of an ambient track with musical, pitch-locked detail instead of generic noise. Lock everything to the track's key and scale (e.g. B minor pentatonic). Generate sporadic random notes from two voices on different patterns: a sine-like 'spray' and a buzzier, brighter 'glass' with tone controls. Set note density with a gravity/rate control, free or tempo-synced from 1/16 up to 16 bars. Add an 'air' white-noise layer and a 'dust' blown-sand noise layer, both of which can be pitch-locked so they take on tonality: air follows spray's pattern and dust follows glass. Move each layer's level with slow LFOs (including smooth random drift). Send it all to a big reverb (size, decay, tone, mix, pre-delay, diffusion, modulation), limit the output, and optionally feed note choices from a slow generative MIDI source. Check the result on a spectrum analyser. This is a generative high-band layer, not a pad or riser.",
 ["Generative note source quantised to a scale (Web Audio: scheduler picking random scale degrees in high octaves → sine and bright oscillators with short envelopes, implementation note)","White-noise layers with tone filters; LFOs incl. smooth random","Long reverb, limiter, spectrum analyser"],
 [("key_scale","string","Track key and scale, e.g. B minor pentatonic",True),("rate","string","Gravity (free) or synced division 1/16 … 16 bars",True),("midi_feed","midi","Optional slow generative MIDI to choose pitches",False)],
 [("high_end_layer","audio","Sparse, pitch-locked chimes/air/dust occupying the high frequencies")],
 ["Pitch-lock is the key feature: all sparkle must be in key so it sounds 'from the same universe'.","Implementing noise pitch-lock as resonant band-pass filters tuned to the chosen notes is an implementation assumption, not stated in the transcript.","Reference-track names and product links are omitted; amounts are by ear.","Keep density low (slow gravity) for 'distant chimes'; fast rates become busy."],
 [("Analyse a reference ambient track's spectrum: note the active, sporadic, pitch-locked detail between ~3 kHz and 20 kHz.","analyse","Target band and density identified"),
  ("Set the key/scale lock to the track (e.g. B minor pentatonic) and trigger the generator; random notes from the scale are sprayed out.","pitch-lock","Sporadic in-key high notes"),
  ("Slow it down with the gravity/rate control so notes arrive slowly; raise the reverb ('glow') amount for long trails. Alternatively switch to tempo sync and choose intervals from 1/16 up to 16 bars.","rate","Slow spring of distant chimes, or grid-locked hits"),
  ("Blend the two tonal voices: spray (standard sine-like tones) and glass (sharper, buzzier shine), each with a tone control and different patterns, so they don't fire together.","voices","Two interleaved chime colours"),
  ("Add the air layer (white noise that 'blows in the distance') and modulate its level with an LFO (e.g. smooth random drift) so it comes and goes. Add the dust layer (sand-scatter-like noise) the same way with the second LFO.","noise layers","Breathing air and dust beneath the chimes"),
  ("Pitch-lock the noise layers: air follows spray's note pattern and dust follows glass, so the noise gains tonality in key.","noise pitch-lock","Noise layers take on in-key pitched colour"),
  ("Shape the reverb (size, decay, tone, mix, pre-delay, diffusion, modulation/chorus), use the output limiter and +6 dB make-up if quiet. Optionally drive pitches from a glacially slow generative MIDI pattern. Then confirm on the full-mix spectrum that the high end is filled.","finish","Full-spectrum ambient mix with musical high-end detail")],
 ["All generated notes belong to the chosen scale.","Spectrum of the mix shows new, sporadic activity above ~3 kHz.","With LFO on air level, the noise audibly drifts in and out.","Synced mode places notes only on the chosen division."],
 ["high-end","ambient","generative","scale-lock","noise","chimes","reverb","web-audio"],
 note="Developer plugin walkthrough; route.py said COVERED but hand-check found no high-band generative sparkle skill. Plugin purchase CTA dropped.")
